WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.980
Dark Phoenix ended an era for the X-Men franchise,
and unfortunately, it didn't end on a high

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:06.980
note.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:11.930
From rotten reviews to disappointing box office
receipts, this superhero sequel is far from

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.820
super, and the writing was on the wall long
before it arrived in theaters.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.120
Here's a spoiler-filled look at why Dark Phoenix
bombed.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:23.120
In late January 2019, Dark Phoenix's test
screenings bombed dramatically.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:26.060
20th Century Fox knew they had to fix it.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.330
But in spite of extensive reshoots, including
major changes to the climax because of perceived

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:35.410
similarities to the ending of another superhero
film, critics still savaged Dark Phoenix,

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:40.550
which earned a Rotten Tomatoes score so low,
it's on par with disasters like 2015's Fantastic

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:45.489
Four, 2004's Catwoman, and the Titanic, not
the movie, the actual ship.

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:49.580
Brian Tallerico at RogerEbert.com summed things
up, simply calling the film

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.820
"...a joyless, lifeless, boring affair."

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.120
That's not good.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.920
Even if critical response had been better,
Dark Phoenix faced an uphill battle at the

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.900
theater thanks to strong competition from
hit films John Wick: Chapter 3, Disney's live

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.159
action remake of Aladdin, and The Secret Life
of Pets 2.

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:11.990
And with box office juggernaut Avengers: Endgame
still in theaters, even superhero fans had

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:12.990
other options.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:17.600
Dark Phoenix could have avoided these problems
if it had debuted in February as originally

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.240
planned, but according to reports, Fox moved
it to make room for another bomb, at least

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.479
domestically, Alita: Battle Angel.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.320
Way to double down, guys.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.960
You could argue that the fate of Dark Phoenix
was sealed way back in December 2017 when

00:01:30.961 --> 00:01:35.149
it was announced that Disney was planning
to acquire 20th Century Fox.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.600
Because that kind of made Dark Phoenix a lame
duck.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.440
"Gross."

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.880
No, not that lame duck.

00:01:45.899 --> 00:01:49.509
But even Howard benefits from being part of
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:52.659
These days, superhero fans love shared universes.

00:01:52.659 --> 00:01:55.969
The idea of bringing the X-Men into the MCU
is exciting.

00:01:55.969 --> 00:02:00.829
But it also made Dark Phoenix seem kind of
pointless, as fans really just want to see

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:04.830
what the new Marvel version of the team is
going to look like, especially since, other

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:09.530
than Logan, the quality of the MCU films has
been so much higher than most of Fox's X-Men

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:10.520
offerings.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:14.630
The X-Men series has had more ups and downs
than a roller coaster.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:19.520
After hitting rock bottom with 2006's X-Men:
The Last Stand, the franchise rebounded in

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:25.110
a big way with the 2011 prequel X-Men: First
Class and its follow-up, 2014's ambitious

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:27.730
time travel epic X-Men: Days of Future Past.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:32.960
But things went sour very fast in 2016 with
X-Men: Apocalypse.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.600
Disappointing fans and critics alike, the
film was poorly received and failed to break

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.250
even at the domestic box office, earning most
of its money overseas.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:44.300
As a result, Dark Phoenix started in a hole
to begin with, as it had to convince viewers

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:48.780
to return to a franchise that had already
disappointed them, and it clearly failed to

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:49.680
do so.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.240
One of the most disappointing aspects of Dark
Phoenix is the relative absence of Quicksilver.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.850
A fan favorite who stole scenes in both Days
of Future Past and Apocalypse, Quicksilver

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:03.050
is sidelined early on in Dark Phoenix and
gets almost no screen time.

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:08.260
There's not even a resolution to the long-running
subplot that he is secretly the son of Magneto.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.180
And then there's the absence of Wolverine.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:14.150
On the one hand, Hugh Jackman made it clear
that he's done playing Logan, so there's basically

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:16.050
no chance he would have been in the film.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:21.020
"Eventually, you're going to hang up the claws,
and it's going to make a lot of people very

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.020
sad."

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.480
"Huh?"

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.820
On the other hand, well…Dark Phoenix really
needed him.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.660
The only real argument otherwise is the fact
that even Jackman couldn't save things the

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.960
last time they made a movie from this story.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.600
Speaking of that...

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:41.400
Dark Phoenix loosely adapts the classic Marvel
storyline "The Dark Phoenix Saga."Sound familiar?

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.600
"It's Phoenix.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:47.200
Phoenix Dark.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:49.560
Dirk.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.960
Phoenix."

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:56.880
Well, if it seems familiar it might be because
the same story was also adapted in 2006's

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:58.890
X-Men: The Last Stand.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:03.910
Yes, despite more than 55 years worth of stories
to choose from, Fox for some reason decided

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:08.819
to adapt the same story twice, even though
The Last Stand was widely disliked by fans

00:04:08.819 --> 00:04:09.990
and critics alike.

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:12.190
Why repeat the same mistake?

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.400
It's just weird.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:19.280
With X-Men premiering in 2000 and Dark Phoenix
acting as the series finale, the X-Men franchise

00:04:19.289 --> 00:04:22.630
is ending as it's just about to turn 20 years
old.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.919
It's arguably ending later than it should
have.

00:04:24.919 --> 00:04:29.789
The box office landscape has changed a lot
since X-Men was first released, and franchise

00:04:29.789 --> 00:04:31.080
fatigue has set in.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:35.150
Marvel has the benefit of multiple franchises;
you don't get tired of the Avengers, because

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:39.210
in between those films you get the Guardians
of the Galaxy, or Black Panther, to mix things

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.210
up.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.500
But at Fox, it's all X-Men all the time.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:47.940
If anything, spinoff hits like Logan and Deadpool
proved just how tired the X-Men formula has

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:52.289
become, as both of those movies succeeded
by intentionally doing something different

00:04:52.289 --> 00:04:54.439
and playing off of expectations.

00:04:54.439 --> 00:04:59.710
Dark Phoenix, on the other hand, is exactly
what you thought, and feared, it was.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:03.891
It's a sad way for the franchise to end, but
it's also a happy occasion for fans to see

00:05:03.891 --> 00:05:06.229
the characters move over to the MCU.

00:05:06.229 --> 00:05:11.469
It's long past due for Marvel's mutants to
come home and realize their full potential.

